<section class="page-head"><div class="wrap">
 <span class="label eyebrow"><a href="/collections/all" class="tlink">SATU</a> · 05 / 08</span>
 <h1 class="disp">The Side Table</h1>
 <p class="pull" style="margin-top:24px">A small square table in repurposed teak, 45 by 45 cm and 45 cm high, made to stand beside a lounger or a chair.</p>
</div></section>
<section><div class="wrap split">
 <div><figure style="margin:0"><img class="pphoto" src="{{ 'sidetable.jpg' | asset_url }}" alt="The Side Table from the front: repurposed teak with a Shou Sugi Ban finish, tapered legs and a three-bolt cluster at each top corner" width="664" height="742"></figure></div>
 <div><dl class="ledger"><div><dt>Collection</dt><dd>SATU</dd></div><div><dt>Category</dt><dd>Table</dd></div><div><dt>Dimensions</dt><dd>L 45 × W 45 × H 45 cm</dd></div><div><dt>Material</dt><dd>Repurposed teak, often from old joglo houses</dd></div><div><dt>Finish</dt><dd>Shou Sugi Ban: flame-darkened teak, finished with natural oil.</dd></div><div><dt>Construction</dt><dd>Modular and knock-down. Assembled on site</dd></div><div><dt>Use</dt><dd>Poolside, terraces and lounges</dd></div><div><dt>Made in</dt><dd>Indonesia</dd></div><div><dt>Price</dt><dd>{% if product.price > 0 %}{{ product.price | money_with_currency }} incl. VAT{% else %}On request{% endif %}</dd></div><div><dt>Delivery</dt><dd>{% if product.price > 0 %}Worldwide. Calculated at checkout{% else %}Worldwide. Confirmed with your quote{% endif %}</dd></div><div><dt>Delivery time</dt><dd>14 weeks from order. Made to order</dd></div><div><dt>Shipping</dt><dd>Flat-packed, assembled on site</dd></div></dl><div style="margin-top:28px">{% render 'buy-box', product: product %}</div></div>
</div></section>
<section><div class="wrap split">
 <div><span class="label eyebrow muted">Details</span><h2 class="disp">About The Side Table.</h2></div>
 <div class="prose"><p>Small enough to stand beside The Sun Lounger or The Lounge Chair, for a drink or a book.</p><p>Like every SATU piece, it travels flat and goes together on site.</p>
 <p>Like every Another Life piece, it is made from timber that already had a first life. Marks from that life stay visible, wherever they don't reduce strength. And if a part ever wears out: replace the part, not the piece.</p></div>
</div></section>

<section class="forest"><div class="wrap split">
 <div><span class="label eyebrow muted">Another Life Passport</span><h2 class="disp">Its own story, one scan away.</h2></div>
 <div class="prose"><p>Each piece carries a QR code that opens its own story: where the wood of The Side Table lived before, who made it, and how to care for it and repair it.</p><p class="cap" style="margin-top:20px"><a href="/pages/passport">About the Passport</a></p></div>
</div></section>
<section><div class="wrap">
 <span class="label eyebrow muted">Pairs with</span>
 <div class="pairs"><a href="/products/the-sun-lounger"><span class="label muted">SATU · 02</span><span class="disp" style="font-size:26px">The Sun Lounger</span><span class="cap">Poolside and outdoors</span></a><a href="/products/the-lounge-chair"><span class="label muted">SATU · 04</span><span class="disp" style="font-size:26px">The Lounge Chair</span><span class="cap">Lounges, lobbies and terraces</span></a></div>
 
</div></section>
